-- title:
--   Closed form of the bordered Hessian form at mu = 0
-- statement:
--   At $\mu = 0$, the bordered form $g^{\mathsf T}\operatorname{adj}(H)\,g$ of the Levi-Civita regularized Hamiltonian is an explicit polynomial $B(s)$ of degree $12$ in $s = (z_1, z_2, w_1, w_2)$, with $82$ monomials, displayed in the statement. Here:
--   - $g = \nabla K$ and $H = \operatorname{Hess}K$;
--   - the adjugate is written through its cofactors, as in the explicit cofactor formula for symmetric $4\times 4$ matrices.
--
--   This polynomial expansion is the input to the fiber reduction, which rewrites $B$ on the energy level set as a trigonometric polynomial in the momentum angle. At $\mu = 0$ every $1/r$ term of the Hamiltonian vanishes, so the identity is purely polynomial.
-- source:
--   Bordered form of the Levi-Civita regularised rotating Kepler Hamiltonian; cf. Grisa, Exact fiber elimination for the Levi–Civita convexity gates of the planar restricted three-body problem, Zenodo 21270420 (2026), Theorem 3.7(b).

